# Normalise line endings to LF in the repository and on checkout.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` (the default in Git for Windows) checks files
# out with CRLF, and `npx prettier --check .` then fails on every file because
# .prettierrc sets `endOfLine: "lf"`. Pinning eol=lf here overrides autocrlf, so a
# clone on Windows matches a clone on the Linux CI runner.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never convert, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
